      "side": 1,
      "message": "The ceiling is `self.retries * bios_job_poll_delay` \u003d 15 * 40 \u003d 600s, so the boot wait rides the generic `RETRIES` (`badfish.py:19`) that also tunes HTTP retries. Each iteration can also spend the 120s request timeout on the jobs collection while holding the move semaphore (`standard.py:184`), so a slow BMC pushes the worst case past 600s. A dedicated attempts constant or a monotonic deadline reads clearer.",
      "revId": "764c7dd747b484c4929d10890330ae801cd41f8e",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
